invariant: INV-36
file: build.zig
catches: test/zig-build-check.sh
reason: build.zig's declarations table names srv_quic.h for the
  tcp-nonblocking server's calls, so the h2 modules include a header that
  declares nothing under their defines and never include
  srv_tcp_nonblocking.h. The objects still export ch_srv_record_init and
  ch_srv_record_in, and the modules declare neither, so a Zig program
  cannot call them. matches.zig's check that the module declares every
  export objects.

--- old
    .{ .header = "srv_tcp_nonblocking.h", .names = &.{ "ch_srv_record_init", "ch_srv_record_in" } },
--- new
    .{ .header = "srv_quic.h", .names = &.{ "ch_srv_record_init", "ch_srv_record_in" } },
